{"step_index":182,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:11:21Z","input_tokens":2871,"cache_read_tokens":79899,"output_tokens":591,"content":"Tarball files for Blender 5.2.0 located:\n\n* **Rofi launcher:** `~/.local/share/applications/blender.desktop`\n* **Binary symlink:** `/usr/local/bin/blender` -> `/opt/blender/blender`\n* **Extracted install directory:** `/opt/blender`\n* **Config directory:** `~/.config/blender/5.2`\n* **Cache:** `~/.cache/blender`\n\nFlatpak 4.5.2 lives separately in `/var/lib/flatpak` and `~/.var/app/org.blender.Blender/` — will remain untouched.\n\n---\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> This permanently deletes the Blender 5.2.0 binaries, desktop launcher, and custom 5.2 configuration/add-ons.\n\nRun in terminal:\n\n```sh\n# 1. Remove Rofi entry (disappears immediately)\nrm -f ~/.local/share/applications/blender.desktop\n\n# 2. Remove binary symlink and extracted tarball\nsudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/blender\nsudo rm -rf /opt/blender\n\n# 3. Remove 5.2 config and cache\nrm -rf ~/.config/blender/5.2 ~/.cache/blender\n```\n\nDone. Only Flatpak version 4.5.2 will remain in Rofi.","thinking":"Investigating the persistence of the \"blender\" entry in the application launcher. The initial assumption is a cached desktop entry; will check rofi's cache update mechanism. Alternatively, deleting the application's desktop file might provide an immediate removal.\n\nExamining the locations where rofi's \"drun\" mode sources desktop files. The system looks in `/usr/share/applications` and `~/.local/share/applications/` to index applications. After deleting the user-specific file, the only remaining entry is from a Flatpak installation path.\n\n\n"}
